00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.340 align:start position:0%
allegations and confirmed instances of  fakery have surrounded the production of  man vs. wild over the years and there  are even some things Bear Grylls and his  producers have admitted to making up so  if you ever thought the show was  unbelievable  you were right let's take a look at all  the reasons man vs. wild is totally fake  although Bear Grylls claims to be a  survival and bushcraft expert a closer  examination shows he wasn't closely  involved in that world before starting  his show which isn't to say he's  completely clueless Grylls was in the  military as a member of the UK's Special  Air Service for three years and as part  of that unit he was trained in combat  survival skills but Grylls didn't come  to prominence for his military exploits  before his big TV break with man vs.  wild in 2006 he became famous for his  widely publicized adventures including  climbing Mount Everest at age 23  crossing the North Atlantic and an  inflatable boat and hosting a dinner  party in a hot-air balloon at 25,000  feet while these were no doubt ruling  experiences they don't necessarily  qualify somebody to be a survival expert  when you compare Grylls his resume to  those a fellow TV survival hosts Ray  Mears and Les Stroud it becomes clear  that his experience pales in comparison  to theirs Mears has taught bushcraft  skills since 1983 to both private  citizens and the military  similarly Stroud has served as a  wilderness survival instructor since  1990 and teaches survival skills to the  Canadian military so while Grylls may  look cool when he heads into the wild  he's not necessarily the one you want  keeping you alive out there  the premise of man vs. wild is one man  alone against the elements but on  several occasions those elements involve  four walls and a roof along with room  service according to survival experts  who worked for the show while filming an  episode in the Sierra Nevada mountains  Grylls enjoyed the nightly hospitality  of the pines resort that past Lake a  modern lodge resorts offering two  on-site restaurants a spa and other  amenities during another episode Grylls  was supposedly stranded on a desert  island that turned out to actually be  Hawaiian archipelago where he again  spent his nights in a local hotel  sometimes  right some guys you gone on I Ont pan  back on many occasions grills has  presented dubious survival techniques  that are actually usable in real life  while filming one episode in a  sweltering locale grills claimed that  you could squeeze and drink water out of  elephant dung Survivorman star and  bushcraft instructor Les Stroud who has  filmed several episodes of his show  among elephants went on record during  the reddit AMA to debunk that technique  he wrote it is not possible to squeeze  drinkable water out of elephant dung  well it is when your cameraman is soaked  it with bottled water in a real survival  situation many of the techniques that  Grylls casually Illustrated on man  versus wild could actually endanger  people and we're not even going to get  into the urine drinking incidents the  worst is even simpler than that  the two dangerous moves that Grylls most  frequently demonstrated on his show  involved hurrying to cross through  dangerous terrain and getting himself  wet when he doesn't have to for those  familiar with the show you know Grylls  hardly ever walked anywhere particularly  when he was on the mountain instead he  ran jumped leapt and swung his way down  cliffs mountain sides and crevices that  may work for a video game hero but in a  true survival situation any injury could  drastically decrease your chances of  making it out alive  a simple broken ankle miles from  civilization could be a death sentence  the smart move is to take your time  finding the safest route it may take  longer but it'll help keep you alive if  you're really in the wild on your own  girls also seems to make a point of  getting wet at every opportunity  he's repelled with vines down waterfalls  gone for swims across frigid Arctic  waters and gone down River Rapids on a  pile of plastic tarp and branches he  called a raft beyond the very real  danger of drowning in such situations or  injuring yourself in a slip or fall  getting wet in the wild is one of the  worst things you can do  hypothermia occurs when the body's core  temperature drops three degrees or more  from normal and it can set in extremely  quickly especially when you're wet on  numerous occasions former crew members  have alleged that entire scenes on man  vs. wild were faked for the viewing  audience in one example a wild mustang  that Grylls attempted to catch and ride  in one episode was really a tame animal  rented from a local trekking lodge in  another episode Grylls leaped OH  chasm of flowing lava which was actually  an illusion created by hot coals lighter  fluid and a smoke machine in another  episode Grylls is shown constructing a  bamboo raft it was later revealed that a  hired expert and the show's crew  actually built the raft for Grylls  before dismantling it so he could be  shown reassembling it on camera after  controversy emerged in 2008 over the  show's less than honest presentation  Grylls and Discovery both apologized for  the fakery deployed on the show girls  told the BBC if people felt misled on  how the first series was represented I'm  really sorry for that the Discovery  Channel only went so far as to admit  that small isolated elements of the show  were fabricated promising viewers that  future seasons would be more transparent  to fulfill that promise a disclaimer was  added at the beginning of each episode  to acknowledge the occasional use of  support crews or fabricated situations  but as much as they tried to diminish it  the message is still the same you just  shouldn't trust what you see on this  show  [Music]
 

